                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>--br-comp-skip-to-pane-surface-border-style</td>
                    <td>var(--br-comp-all-area-header-border-style:)</td>
                    <td>The border style - uses the shared component variable.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>--br-comp-skip-to-pane-surface-border-width</td>
                    <td>var(--br-comp-all-outline-offset)</td>
                    <td>
                        The border width - <b>does not use the shared component variable</b> It uses the outline offset as its using
                        an outline without an offset. In this instance the border is the acting as an offset.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>--br-comp-skip-to-pane-surface-border-colour</td>
                    <td>var(--br-unit-colour-canvas)</td>
                    <td>The border colour - <b>does not use the shared component variable.</b></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>--br-comp-skip-to-pane-surface-border-radius-top-right</td>
                    <td>var(--br-unit-radius-5)</td>
                    <td>The border radius of the top right corner - <b>no shared variable so uses the unit value directly.</b></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>--br-comp-skip-to-pane-surface-border-radius-top-left</td>
                    <td>var(--br-unit-radius-5)</td>
                    <td>The border radius of the top left corner - <b>no shared variable so uses the unit value directly.</b></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
